  "id": "monaural",
  "term": "monaural",
  "definition": "Monaural refers to sound presented within a single auditory channel, so that two nearby frequencies are combined before reaching the listener. Their overlap produces a perceived rhythmic beat at the difference between the two frequencies, and this can be delivered to one ear or to both ears at the same time.",
